# Restart the app yourself

If rust, SQL, migrations, the native menu, or a command the running exe has not loaded changed, restart in the same turn.

1. Write `%LOCALAPPDATA%\com.finos.desktop\restart.token` with an ISO stamp and a reason. Delete `%LOCALAPPDATA%\com.finos.desktop\page-loaded.log` in the same step so an old Home line cannot pass.
2. Stop every `finos-desktop` so repo-root `finos.bat` starts one `finos (dev)` child. Do not start `start-finos-dev.bat` alone. Do not `npm run desktop:build`.
3. Run `.\scripts\app-up.ps1`. It exits 0 only when exactly one `finos-desktop.exe` is running, exactly one `start-finos-dev.bat` launcher is running, and `page loaded Home` is newer than that process. `http://localhost:1420` answering is not proof. A second desktop or a second dev launcher is a failed turn.
4. Read `%LOCALAPPDATA%\com.finos.desktop\dev-console.log`. `panicked`, `Failed to setup`, or `npm error` is a failed turn. A window full of errors is not complete. The same sentences are checked by `app-up.ps1`.
5. If the parent is missing, start repo-root `finos.bat` only.

Do not leave File → Restart as owner homework.
